# Spark Sensor And Uplink Workflow

This live template uses a fictional sensor API. It provisions a synthetic
sensor, posts two readings in the previous completed UTC hour, and checks the
readings and their delta. The hourly-summary check is optional.

See the README for the ignored demo configuration and how to run against a
disposable test API.

```yaml
include:
  - sensor-uplink-demo.private.yaml
```

```yaml
variables:
  demo_host: $env:RESTY_SPARK_DEMO_HOST
  hour_end: ${{ start_of_hour(utc_now()) }}
  hour_start: ${{ hour_end - hours(1) }}
  first_read_time: ${{ hour_start + minutes(10) }}
  second_read_time: ${{ hour_start + minutes(50) }}
  first_kwh: 1000.0
  expected_kwh_delta: 1.25
  second_kwh: ${{ first_kwh + expected_kwh_delta }}
  sensor_ref: ${{ random_hex(16) }}
  first_reading_id: ${{ uuid() }}
  second_reading_id: ${{ uuid() }}
  verify_hourly_summary: false
```

## Discover Or Provision The Sensor

```yaml
test: spark-sensor-lookup
get: $demo_host/demo/devices/$sensor_ref
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
expect:
  status: [200, 404]
capture:
  sensor_lookup_status: $response.status
```

```yaml
test: spark-sensor-create
requires: spark-sensor-lookup
when: ${{ sensor_lookup_status == 404 }}
post: $demo_host/demo/devices
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
body:
  label: DEMO-$sensor_ref
  group: $demo_sensor_group
  reference: $sensor_ref
expect:
  status: 201
```

```yaml
test: spark-sensor-ready
requires:
  - spark-sensor-lookup
  - spark-sensor-create
get: $demo_host/demo/devices/$sensor_ref
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
expect:
  status: 200
capture:
  sensor_id: $.fixture.id
retry:
  attempts: 8
  delay: ${{ milliseconds(500) }}
  backoff: fixed
  statuses: [404, 409, 500, 502, 503, 504]
```

## Post Two Synthetic Readings

```yaml
test: spark-uplink-first
requires: spark-sensor-ready
post: $demo_host/demo/telemetry
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
body:
  sensorId: $sensor_id
  readingId: $first_reading_id
  recordedAt: $first_read_time
  kilowattHours: $first_kwh
expect:
  status: 204
```

```yaml
test: spark-uplink-second
requires: spark-uplink-first
post: $demo_host/demo/telemetry
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
body:
  sensorId: $sensor_id
  readingId: $second_reading_id
  recordedAt: $second_read_time
  kilowattHours: $second_kwh
expect:
  status: 204
```

## Verify Raw Reads First

```yaml
test: spark-kwh-reads
requires: spark-uplink-second
get: $demo_host/demo/devices/$sensor_id/readings?from=$hour_start&until=$hour_end
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
expect:
  status: 200
  values:
    - key: $.fixture.reads.length()
      op: greater_than
      value: 1
retry:
  attempts: 12
  delay: ${{ seconds(1) }}
  backoff: fixed
  statuses: [404, 409, 500, 502, 503, 504]
  expectation_failures: true
```

```yaml
test: spark-kwh-delta
requires: spark-kwh-reads
get: $demo_host/demo/devices/$sensor_id/reading-delta?from=$hour_start&until=$hour_end
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
expect:
  status: 200
  values:
    - key: $.fixture.delta
      op: equals
      value: $expected_kwh_delta
retry:
  attempts: 12
  delay: ${{ seconds(1) }}
  backoff: fixed
  statuses: [404, 409, 500, 502, 503, 504]
  expectation_failures: true
```

## Optionally Verify The Precomputed Hourly Summary

Set `verify_hourly_summary` to `true` when the disposable API provides this endpoint.

```yaml
test: spark-hourly-kwh-delta
requires: spark-kwh-delta
when: ${{ verify_hourly_summary }}
get: $demo_host/demo/devices/$sensor_id/hourly-summary?from=$hour_start&until=$hour_end
headers:
  authorization: $demo_authorization
expect:
  status: 200
  values:
    - key: $.fixture.delta
      op: equals
      value: $expected_kwh_delta
retry:
  attempts: 12
  delay: ${{ seconds(5) }}
  backoff: fixed
  statuses: [404, 409, 500, 502, 503, 504]
  expectation_failures: true
```
